  "summary": "Discover a unique sweet tradition with this fragrant <b>Lebanese dessert stew</b>, which highlights tender simmered pumpkin in a fragrant syrup. Soft <b>sugar pumpkin</b> cubes absorb warm notes of cinnamon, cloves, and floral orange blossom water as they cook down into a glossy, amber-hued syrup. Unlike savory stews, this dish is crafted specifically to end a festive meal on a delicate, aromatic note. Once chilled or brought to room temperature, the candied pumpkin offers a silky melt-in-your-mouth texture that pairs beautifully with rich Lebanese clotted cream, known as ashta. A generous sprinkling of lightly toasted pine nuts and slivered almonds adds an inviting crunch and nutty depth. Easy to prepare ahead of time, this elegant sweet course showcases how classic Levantine spices elevate humble garden vegetables into a sophisticated dessert fit for holiday celebrations and family gatherings alike.",
